91c8b8a1a9","e20ff9851238356c","e4a3a4d91ce8e8ce","e4c6d205df2cfd78","e50bc1a1fbf870cc","e524a805da015d5e","e59e69e8065ae145","e62b97dba9a9151f","e6e8a880ab617f48","e6e8a880ab617f48","e77b7dd7fdd4932d","e9000a98c5d98f68","ea85f610b571c068","eb8d126e5a3af51e","ec02528fa90f511f","ed559f00d7e176c2","ef7152669b92fa28","efcd923c494b0e34","f093c30f71db28e3","f2ea33c193af0c2d","f4dbf639ed3f31fd","f732cb0ceaf8ebdc","f89ef26c2f702dbd","f8bce5b6361890c8","fa03100d1426cdc3","fa2b4f17f4588975","faa26d2df34adf5e","fb29329679909007","fb57956b70681d45","fca455e56ff45da0","fcfa9f2350a8fefb","fd7b247509536744","fda58aa25ca91f64","ff609eca4d866eb7"],"groups":["4286d11458512083","cf591cf19f5e0b5b","ec88684a7bf54524","557ffbad658b2328","9e2f0cb35381f1c0","6fbe936c813dfb9a","fdc5b6f9a80aa4ec","67ffa4d5b4bac836","0a758c6afad1ddbd","6ce313850f0594e0","d0f4eb4c7c675ffc"],"findings":"**Review of the decision-records change**\n\nI ran the decision test file (7/7 pass) and reproduced one mismatch in a scratch repo under `/tmp/git-gud-UQujdG/scratch/by/r`. The other points come from reading the code.\n\n**1. Mismatches**\n\n- **`decide-cli` / `decision-records`: overlong `--by` is accepted, then silently dropped. Verified.** `checkDecision` validates `finding` and `note` but not `by`. The reader rejects any decision whose `by` is over 200 characters (`r.by.length <= 200`). I ran `reviews HEAD --decide <id> --finding 1 --outcome fixed --by <250 chars>`. It printed `recorded \"1\": fixed on 1 commit` and exited 0. The next `reviews HEAD` showed `decisions on this review: none yet`. The write reports success for a record that can never be read. The README's \"lines … are ignored\" wording doesn't cover this, since the caller gets no error. Fix: apply a `by` length check in `checkDecision` with the same message style as the others.\n- **`decision-display`: the `show` summary covers more than the stated scope. Read.** `reviewsLine` in `show.ts` takes `complete` from the open (non-clean) reviews, but `decisionSummary` counts every decision on the commit, including decisions on clean reviews. A commit with a clean review that has decisions, plus one open review that is complete, shows \"N … · complete\" with N inflated by the clean review's decisions. The per-review `reviews` view doesn't have this problem.\n- **`decision-records`: the 16 KB guard does not cover the existing reader. Read.** The notes say \"Lines over 16 KB are skipped before parsing\". That holds only in `readDecisions`. `readDecisions` calls `readReviews`, which still runs `JSON.parse` on every line with no length cap. The hostile test's 10 MB junk line is therefore still parsed on each `reviews`, `show` and `carry`, and the wording overstates the protection. The test passes, but it does not show the cost is bounded.\n\n**2. Misgraded necessity**\n\n- `decision-follow` (required) and `decision-display` (required) are fair. They are what the task asks for.\n- `decision-docs` (supporting, serves `decision-records`) is reasonable. It also serves the user-facing CLI, so \"supporting\" is slightly low, but this does not change the verdict.\n- The `plain(r.findings, true)` change in `decision-display` (h7) sanitises the existing review findings output, not decisions. It is disclosed in the notes, but it is a behaviour change outside \"decisions\" and could sit in its own group, or be labelled incidental.\n\n**3. Removal candidates**\n\n- None of the required groups can be dropped without failing the task.\n- The `plain()` call on review findings (h7) could be deferred to its own change. Impact: none on decisions, and one less change to review the display of.\n\n**4. Simplifications**\n\n- `readDecisions` calls `readReviews(sha)` internally, and `reviewsLine` and `copyReviews` call both. The same note is parsed two or three times per call. Passing the review list in, or having one function return both, avoids this.\n- `decisionSummary`'s `complete` default (`ds.some(d => d.complete)`) and the explicit `complete` argument in `reviewsLine` mean different things. A single explicit parameter would be clearer.\n- `checkDecision` could take `by` as well, which would put the write-side limits in one place and remove the mismatch in item 1.\n\n**5. Missing risks**\n\n- The overlong `--by` silent drop (item 1). Not in the author's risk list.\n- Unbounded `readReviews` parsing of large junk lines (item 1, read).\n- `show` summary scope (item 1, read).\n- The `--record`, `--stamp` and `--decide` flags are not mutually exclusive. With `--record --finding …` the decision flags are silently ignored, because the `--record` branch returns before the decision check. Read only, minor.\n\nChecked and consistent: `readReviews` is unchanged, as the notes say; `cat_sort_uniq` is used for sync merges (`sync.ts:162,179`); `notes.rewriteRef` is set in `init.ts:96`; the 7 decision tests pass.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
