880ab617f48","e6e8a880ab617f48","e77b7dd7fdd4932d","e9000a98c5d98f68","ea85f610b571c068","eb8d126e5a3af51e","ec02528fa90f511f","ed559f00d7e176c2","ef7152669b92fa28","efcd923c494b0e34","f093c30f71db28e3","f1f00957ac93f821","f2ea33c193af0c2d","f4dbf639ed3f31fd","f732cb0ceaf8ebdc","f89ef26c2f702dbd","f8bce5b6361890c8","fa03100d1426cdc3","fa2b4f17f4588975","faa26d2df34adf5e","fb29329679909007","fb57956b70681d45","fca455e56ff45da0","fcfa9f2350a8fefb","fd7b247509536744","fda58aa25ca91f64","ff609eca4d866eb7"],"groups":["4286d11458512083","cf591cf19f5e0b5b","ec88684a7bf54524","557ffbad658b2328","9e2f0cb35381f1c0","6fbe936c813dfb9a","fdc5b6f9a80aa4ec","67ffa4d5b4bac836","0a758c6afad1ddbd","d0f4eb4c7c675ffc"],"findings":"I only read the change. I did not run it or the tests, so every finding below is **read**.\n\n1. **`src/reviews.ts` `plain` (group `decision-records`)**: the `multiline` flag duplicates a long control-character regex with one small difference. Build the shared class once and add `\\n\\t` handling only when `multiline` is set. For example, keep one `const BAD = '\\\\x00-\\\\x1f\\\\x7f-\\\\x9f\\\\u2028…'`, then use `new RegExp(`[${BAD}]`, 'g')` and `multiline ? text.replace(/[^\\S]…/)`. A simpler option is to split on `\\n`, sanitise each line with the single-line regex, and rejoin. This is about 5 lines changed. A future edit to the bidi or control ranges can then no longer miss one of the two copies.\n\n2. **Repeated note reads (`src/reviews.ts` `readDecisions`, `src/commands/reviews.ts`, `src/commands/show.ts`, `copyReviews`)**: for each commit, `readDecisions` runs `git notes show` and then calls `readReviews`, which reads the same note again.\n   - `reviewStatus` presumably reads the note a third time.\n   - `reviews --decide` calls `readReviews` for every sha, and again for every sha on the error path.\n   - `copyReviews` does `from.flatMap(readReviews)` and `from.flatMap(readDecisions)`, so it reads each source's reviews twice.\n   - Over a range of N commits this is about 3–4 git spawns per commit.\n   - Fix: add one `readNote(sha)` that returns `{reviews, decisions}` from a single note read. Alternatively, let `readDecisions(sha, reviews = readReviews(sha))` take the reviews as an optional argument.\n   - This is about 15 lines. It would mainly help `reviews` on a long range and `show`.\n\n3. **`src/commands/show.ts` `reviewsLine`**: the `decided` expression is hard to read. It combines `open.length || decisions.length`, then `open.length > 0 && open.every(... d.complete)`, and passes the result as `decisionSummary`'s `complete` argument. This repeats the per-review \"is it complete\" logic from `commands/reviews.ts`.\n   - Fix: add a small helper in `reviews.ts`, such as `openReviews(reviews, decisions)` or `allArbitrated(...)`. Both places can then share it, and `reviewsLine` becomes two lines.\n   - This is about 10 lines. It makes the \"complete\" rule live in one place.\n\n4. **`src/commands/reviews.ts` `--decide` block (group `decide-cli`)**: the block is about 28 lines inline in `run()`, and `run()` already handles `--record` and `--stamp`.\n   - Move it into `function decide(values, positionals, shas)` and move the `--complete` conflict check into `checkDecision`. That function then covers both modes, so validation is in one place.\n   - Also, the trailing loop that rejects stray `--finding`, `--outcome` and the other flags runs after the `--decide` return. It can fold into the same function.\n   - This is a refactor of about 30 lines with no behaviour change.\n\n5. **`src/reviews.ts` `readDecisions` validation**: the boolean chain with the nested ternary is dense, and it mixes `str('at')` with length checks that come after it.\n   - Extract `isValidDecision(r, ids): r is DecisionRecord`, and use early returns for the `complete` and finding cases.\n   - Also, `[...new Set(raw.split('\\n'))]` dedupes lines only. Two decisions that differ only in whitespace or key order still count twice. That matches the a